in @prism
in @meta
in @epistemologic/property/content_addressed

# @uuid — the universal 128-bit identifier discipline.
#
# Root prism in the substrate, declared in the floor alongside
# @prism, @nl, @metalogue, @glass. Names the universal identifier
# carrier: a 128-bit value whose canonical string form is the
# hyphenated 8-4-4-4-12 (36-character) representation.
#
# === Why @uuid is a root prism ===
#
# Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] every kind that
# stands on its own algebra is a prism. UUIDs ARE such a kind: a
# 128-bit address space with a single string discipline (hyphenated
# form), parse / format / equality as the universal surface, and
# multiple specializations that each carry their own structural
# meaning under the same address space. The root prism declares the
# discipline; sub-prisms declare the variants.
#
# Variants the substrate currently knows or will pull through:
#   @uuid/spectral   the navigable spectral identifier; 48 ACTIVE +
#                    80 DARK; monoid w.r.t. shard merge
#                    (shards/uuid/spectral.mirror, 2026-06-06
#                    Mara's tick — the first sub-prism to land).
#   @uuid/v4         random; opaque; for when an identifier needs
#                    to be drawn without spectral structure. Lands
#                    when a consumer pulls.
#   @uuid/v7         timestamp-leading; sortable by issuance time.
#                    Lands when a consumer pulls.
#   @uuid/nil        the all-zeros constant; not a variant so much
#                    as the bottom of the address space. Lands when
#                    a consumer pulls.
#
# === What the root declares vs. what variants declare ===
#
# Root @uuid declares the universal contract — the 128-bit address
# space, the canonical string form, parse / format / equality. No
# monoid; that's variant-specific (only @uuid/spectral forms one).
# No structural fields; the carrier IS opaque at the root. The
# variants below declare structure when their semantics require it
# (e.g. @uuid/spectral splits into active + dark; v4 has no structure
# at all).
#
# === The carrier ===
#
# `type uuid = ref` per the no-bare-types discipline. A typed
# reference whose content IS its byte content. Two uuids are equal
# iff their byte content is byte-equal. The structural meaning of
# the 128 bits is variant-defined.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md §4.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Related shards: uuid/spectral.mirror (the first sub-prism),
#                 glass.mirror (shard.id IS @uuid/spectral),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (oid + shard_ref consumers).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/uuid.mirror`
# declares `@uuid` and only that.

# The universal 128-bit identifier carrier.
#
# A typed reference whose content IS its identity. Construction is
# variant-specific (v4: random; v7: timestamp + random; spectral:
# from_parts(active, dark)); equality at the root is byte-equality
# of the resulting reference.
type uuid = ref

# === Surface: parse / format / equality ===
#
# parse(text) -> imperfect
#   Parse the hyphenated string form into a uuid value. imperfect
#   carries the parsed uuid on success, opacity on failure (wrong
#   length, non-hex digit, hyphens at wrong positions). The 36-char
#   canonical form is what every variant emits and accepts; variants
#   MAY add their own parsers but the root contract is the
#   hyphenated form.
parse(text: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

# format(u) -> ref
#   Format the uuid as the 36-character hyphenated string. Stable
#   across variants: a v4 and a spectral uuid with byte-equal carriers
#   format identically. The lowercase form per RFC 4122 / RFC 9562.
format(u: uuid) -> ref { \ }

# equals(a, b) -> verdict
#   Byte-equality on the 128-bit carrier. Same uuid (variant-
#   independent) iff byte-equal. Variants MAY add stronger
#   equivalences (e.g. spectral's monoid idempotency means
#   combine(a, a) = a, which IS byte-equality of the carriers); the
#   root equality is the byte test.
equals(a: uuid, b: uuid) -> verdict { \ }

# === Properties ===
#
# content_addressed(uuid)
#   The 128-bit carrier IS its identity. Two uuids are the same uuid
#   iff their byte content is byte-equal. Foundational; every variant
#   inherits this property. The variants' structural meaning (active /
#   dark for spectral; random for v4) lives on top.
requires content_addressed(uuid)

out @uuid
out uuid
out parse
out format
out equals
